<title>LEBANON: LEBANON BYBLOS BANK MID-YEAR RESULTS.</title>
<headline>LEBANON BYBLOS BANK MID-YEAR RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lebanon's Byblos Bank said on Tuesday that its unaudited mid-year net profits after tax rose 41.2 percent to 23.015 billion pounds ($15 million).</p>
<p>The bank issued the following results and highlights for the six months ended June 30 (in millions of Lebanese pounds unless otherwise stated):</p>
<p>			   Unaudited	  Unaudited	  Unaudited</p>
<p>			     1997		 1996		  1995</p>
<p>  Total assets	 2,562,245	  1,870,417	  1,424,178</p>
<p>  Customer deposits  2,115,551	  1,583,669	  1,230,252</p>
<p>  Customer advances    822,536	    631,050	    452,170</p>
<p>  Tier one capital     143,990	    105,345	     43,224</p>
<p>  Tier two capital	36,218	     21,102	     14,585</p>
<p>  Net interest income   47,857	     40,574	     25,890</p>
<p>  Net non interest inc.  6,288		5,537		3,700</p>
<p>  Operating expenses    27,477	     24,152	     18,821</p>
<p>  Net income		23,015	     16,293		8,500</p>
<p>  Earning per share	  418		  296		  154</p>
<p>  Book value per share   2,742		2,040		  785</p>
<p>Growth</p>
<p>    Assets		    15.47%	    13.26%	    15.92%</p>
<p>    net customer advances 18.68%	    21.00%	    19.57%</p>
<p>    customer deposits     15.66%	    13.66%	    16.54%</p>
<p>Profitability</p>
<p>    ROA			1.93%		 1.85%	     1.28%</p>
<p>    ROE		     32.38%		30.40%	    42.41%</p>
<p>    Net interest margin  4.24%		 4.94%	     4.17%</p>
<p>    Cost-to-income	50.75%		52.38%	    63.60%</p>
<p>Liquidity</p>
<p>Liquid assets to</p>
<p>    total assets	  62.50%		60.28%	    62.06%</p>
<p>Capitalisation</p>
<p>    Capital to assets    7.03%		 6.76%	     4.06%</p>
<p>  $1 =			 1,540		1,571	     1,621</p>
<p>-- Beirut editorial (9611)  745307  745308  602057</p>
</text>
